## What does Storybook add?

**Layout, and only layout.** Storybook is built from the other two: each pattern takes a schema's fields and the tokens' values and arranges them on a page. That arrangement is the one thing Storybook has the final word on.

{% endmarkdown %}
<aside class="kh-scrolly__define" data-define="nSB"><p><strong><dfn>Storybook</dfn>:</strong> the developers' working catalogue of every component, running live in the browser with all its variations.</p></aside>
{% markdown %}

**The Book Card shows the split.** Its four presets, including a version without an image, come from the schema, and its colour, type and spacing from the tokens. Where the boxes land is Storybook's call, and an automated geometry check measures against it.

**Everything after this depends on that split.** Each source owns one question, so each can be checked on that question alone.

{% endmarkdown %}
