## How is the Figma library built?

{% endmarkdown %}
<aside class="kh-scrolly__define" data-define="nF"><p><strong><dfn>Figma</dfn>:</strong> where designers mock up pages. Its library is the shared set of ready-made components they drag into their designs.</p></aside>
{% markdown %}

**The plugin asks each source the question it owns.** Field lists and presets come from the schemas, values bind to Figma variables generated from the tokens, and geometry is checked against Storybook. Nothing in the library is authored in Figma: a designer switching the Book Card to its no-image preset is choosing one the schema already allows.

**AI coding agents wrote most of the plugin, and the structure gave their work a right answer.** The agents traced tokens through the code and generated the build instructions for each component, and every instruction could be checked against one of the three sources. Their output still had errors. The difference was that I could trace each one.

{% endmarkdown %}
